  "passage": {
    "text": "Some agricultural products go to other countries. We call this export. Lithuania exports wheat, milk and cheese to many markets. Other products come from abroad. We call this import. We import bananas and oranges because they cannot grow in our climate. Export is good for farmers because they find more customers. But every country has its own rules and standards for food. Last week a truck with cheese waited at the border for two days. The driver was tired and the cheese was not fresh. Farmers want faster and simpler trade rules.",
